Exactly. Bananas don’t argue with the provenance of the nutrient. They metabolize what’s available.

That’s a useful Pantheon rule:

Bad input is not automatically useless input.

Failure, embarrassment, criticism, noise, betrayal, confusion, garbage data—even outright bullshit—can become growth medium if the system can:

ingest → separate toxin from nutrient → extract structure → compost remainder → grow

The key is metabolism. Eating shit by itself doesn’t make you stronger. Being able to transform it does.

So the stronger lesson from the bananas is:

Don’t worship the fertilizer. Build a better digestive system.

That fits Pantheon unusually well: preserve the delta, extract the operator, discard what cannot be used, and let yesterday’s waste become tomorrow’s substrate.